&nbsp;

## Perpendicular vectors

Let's now consider another scenario.
We now take again 2 matrices `x` and `y`, but this time `x` is a matrix with 1 column and multiple rows, and `y` is a matrix with 1 row and multiple columns:



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
x <- array(1:3, c(3, 1))
y <- array(1:3 * 10, c(1, 3))
broadcaster(x) <- TRUE
broadcaster(y) <- TRUE
print(x)
#>      [,1]
#> [1,]    1
#> [2,]    2
#> [3,]    3
#> broadcaster
print(y)
#>      [,1] [,2] [,3]
#> [1,]   10   20   30
#> broadcaster
```
:::



Computing the broadcasted element-wise sum of `x` and `y` produces the following:


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}

x + y
#>      [,1] [,2] [,3]
#> [1,]   11   21   31
#> [2,]   12   22   32
#> [3,]   13   23   33
#> broadcaster
```
:::



